---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../consts';
---

<PageLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="Honest Picture's privacy policy: we do not store or transmit your assessment answers, we do not require accounts, and we are transparent about the limited data we collect."
  path="/privacy-policy"
  eyebrow="Trust & Legal"
  heading="Privacy Policy"
  lede="The short version: your assessment answers never leave your browser, we do not require an account, and we collect as little as possible."
  updated="June 2026"
>
  <h2>The principle</h2>
  <p>
    {SITE.name} is built so that the most sensitive thing you do here — answering
    honest questions about your life — happens entirely on your own device. We
    designed it this way on purpose. A site about seeing your life clearly should
    not quietly harvest it.
  </p>

  <h2>Your assessment answers</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Your answers are processed <strong>only in your browser</strong> to generate your context picture.</li>
    <li>They are <strong>not stored</strong> on our servers, in a database, or in your browser’s local storage.</li>
    <li>They are <strong>not transmitted</strong> to us or to any third party.</li>
    <li>They are <strong>not linked</strong> to your identity, because we never ask for it.</li>
    <li>When you close or refresh the page, your answers are gone.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What we do collect</h2>
  <p>
    Like most websites, we may collect limited, standard technical information to
    keep the site working and understand aggregate usage:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Basic analytics.</strong> If analytics are enabled, we use them to
      understand aggregate, anonymised traffic — which pages are read, roughly how
      many people visit. This never includes your assessment answers. See
      <a href="/how-we-use-data">how we use data</a> for specifics.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Server logs.</strong> Our hosting provider may keep standard logs
      (e.g. IP address, browser type) for security and reliability, as is normal
      for any website.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Cookies and advertising</h2>
  <p>
    The site currently runs without advertising. If we introduce advertising
    through Google AdSense in the future, third-party vendors including Google may
    use cookies to serve ads based on prior visits, in line with Google’s
    policies. At that point this section will be updated to describe those cookies
    and how to opt out, and where required we will request consent before
    non-essential cookies are set. You will always be able to manage ad
    personalisation through
    <a href="https://www.google.com/settings/ads" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">Google’s Ads Settings</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>
    This site is intended for adults and is not directed at children under 13 (or
    the applicable age in your jurisdiction). We do not knowingly collect personal
    information from children.
  </p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    Because we do not build profiles or store your answers, there is generally no
    personal dataset about you for us to export or delete. If you have emailed us
    and want that correspondence removed, contact us and we will handle it. Depending
    on where you live, you may have rights under laws such as the GDPR or CCPA; we
    aim to honour those rights.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>
    We may update this policy as the site evolves. Material changes will be
    reflected in the "last updated" date above.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about privacy? Email <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>
    or see our <a href="/contact">contact page</a>.
  </p>
</PageLayout>
